    "scope": "Fix baseline-extract compression and pinned-baseline reproduction in issue486 evidence packet; preserve original archives/records; no shared dataset changes"
  },
  "acceptance_text": "Raised: 2026-10-03 UTC. Moderator finding on PR #604, merge `276d72e1f316ad58d52c8fea7974a873c2ec9387`; parent packet #486, integrator #488.\n\nREADME calls extract_baseline.py deterministic and instructs readers to run it first. That script writes sources/current-scope-and-parents.geojson.gz and current-parent-chains.json.gz using gzip.open(...,'wb',compresslevel=9) without a fixed recorded timestamp. Python embeds current time in the gzip header by default, so identical input rerun at a different second changes both retained compressed SHA-256 values. The script updates baseline-extract-receipt.json, while sources.json still binds the original compressed hashes. It also reads current main without checking that hierarchy/footprint/frozen-scope hashes still match the assigned v5 baseline before overwriting the retained extracts. These are reproducibility/provenance defects, not evidence of a wrong geographic boundary. The moderator inspected code and receipts but did not execute the script.\n\nOne focused evidence/reproduction correction. Coordinate with original packet owner before reserving its directory. Preserve original extracts, hashes, source bytes, 211 IDs and dated history. Establish a deterministic, pinned reproduction method: either restore recorded compression metadata when reproducing original bytes, or produce separately identified artifacts with canonical uncompressed hashes and explicitly retain original archives. Reject a changed baseline before overwriting anything; do not silently repin or replace immutable evidence. Reconcile README, receipts and source registry and add a meaningful two-run/check and wrong-baseline rejection check.\n\nNo shared hierarchy/geometry/grid/application/live data/certificate changes or geographic approval. Complete acceptance is reproducible, honestly labeled artifacts with retained original provenance and consistent hashes; no historical imports enabled.\n\n",
